From 9e6ab61fcee8f1ebaf21098c8855fce7e6c43aca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:06:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GUI G1: the no-command-line control panel

tools/launcher.py (stdlib-only Python 3) + web/gui.html put the whole CLI
surface on one page: machine setup (boot path, platform, SMP, LPC/USB, the
two SATA controllers, VBE, TAP networking with a managed tap_responder.py,
run limits, artifact toggles, debug options), run control (start/restart/
stop, pause/continue/step, breakpoints, scancodes and typing), the live
view (framebuffer + PNG export, registers, vCPUs, log, the x86dbg REPL),
named snapshots (savevm/loadvm behind buttons), per-run artifact download
and named config presets -- all in Russian, no shell required.

The launcher builds argv strictly from its option SCHEMA (choice/regex/
int-range/existing-path; unknown keys and injected values refused -- the
tests pin ten rejection NCs including "platform: haswell; rm -rf /"),
runs each machine exactly like the CLI (argv list, cwd = repo root) with
--monitor=127.0.0.1:<free port>, and splices the RFC 6455 monitor protocol
through /ws with two independent relay pumps.  Measured defect fixed in
the splice: the single-loop relay dropped a pending quit command when the
client vanished mid-keyframe (one direction's sendall failure killed the
other).

T5 end-stop semantics kept: at the post-mortem stop the page keeps the
final state visible and "Stop" sends the monitor's quit first, so the
emulator prints stats/receipts and writes artifacts (SIGTERM is the
fallback).  Windows: build.bat gui, gui.bat double-click, x86emu.exe
discovery, killpg-free process termination.

Gates: tests/test_gui_launcher.py (41 vectors: schema + argv shape,
HTTP surface, lifecycle through the proxy -- 101 handshake, state push,
continue, end stop, quit -> exit 0 -> GUEST_OK + PPM artifacts -- and the
502/404/traversal refusals) wired into make test and make test-sanitize;
make test 597 ok / 0 FAIL, ASan+UBSan clean, fuzz 12288 states match.
savevm/loadvm round trip measured live through the GUI path.
